review_comments.body:
Doesn't support package sets yet (and `genAttrs` is vaguely a code smell).

I feel like an attrset literal would be the right kind of boilerplate, because it's easy enough to write, yet flexible with what it can do.

```suggestion
pkgs:
# A list of all packages that define service modules, used for documentation rendering.
# Pairs *attribute path* to package that defines it.
# E.g. "pythonPackages.foo" = pkgs.pythonPackages.foo;
{
  "ghostunnel" = pkgs.ghostunnel;
  "ktls-utils" = pkgs.ktls-utils;
  "php" = pkgs.php;
  "snid" = pkgs.snid;
}
```

This is so beginner users don't get confused and it is valid syntax.

```suggestion
{ pkgs, ...}: 
{
  system.services.my-service-instance = {
    imports = [ pkgs.some-application.services.some-service-module ];
    foo.settings = {
      # ...
    };
  };
}
```
